Open the Heap Dump (.hprof) and there are essentially 4 views of interest:

[a] Thread View
Threads with their stack and frame variables

[b] Dominator View
To debug leaks (who is keeping whom alive)

[c] Class Histogram
How many instances of each class type along with shallow and retained heap sizes

[d] OQL
To use your own queries

All of these can be found in the icon list when you open the heap dump (refer to the attached image)

